Here’s the deﬁnition of std::cmp::PartialEq:

 trait PartialEq<Rhs = Self> where Rhs: ?Sized, { fn eq(&self, other: &Rhs) -> bool; fn ne(&self, other: &Rhs) -> bool { !self.eq(other) } }

Since the ne method has a default deﬁnition, you only need to deﬁne eq to implement the PartialEq trait, so here’s a complete implementation for Complex:

 impl<T: PartialEq> PartialEq for Complex<T> { fn eq(&self, other: &Complex<T>) -> bool { self.re == other.re && self.im == other.im } }

In other words, for any component type T that itself can be compared for equality, this implements comparison for Complex<T>. Assuming we’ve also implemented

