While PartialOrd is what you’ll usually see, total orderings deﬁned with Ord are necessary in some cases, such as the sorting methods implemented in the standard library. For example, sorting intervals isn’t possible with only a PartialOrd implementation. If you do want to sort them, you’ll have to ﬁll in the gaps of the unordered cases. You might want to sort by upper bound, for instance, and it’s easy to do that with sort_by_key:

